      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto (eighth section of join)",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>in the air of the heaven like a bird.</li>\n<li>R. Yehudah the gardener said to R. Yehoshu\u02bfa:</li>\n<li>&ldquo;My master, shall we go after him?&rdquo; He said to him: &ldquo;Go.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>At that moment R. Yehudah purified</li>\n<li>himself, and said the Ineffable Name, and flew up after him.</li>\n<li>When Yeshu saw R. Yehudah</li>\n<li>behind him, he went and hid himself in the cave of</li>\n<li>Elijah, and he said words of a spell, and</li>\n<li>the mouth of the cave was shut. (some words omitted) And he said thus: &ldquo;Opening, opening,</li>\n<li>open up! For I am the messenger of the Holy One, blessed be He.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>When the opening of the cave heard this,</li>\n<li>it opened up. Yeshu the wicked made</li>\n<li>[himself? like] a rooster, and went&nbsp;</li>\n<li>[and sat?] on Mount Carmel. And</li>\n<li>R. [Yehudah] the gardener came and held him by his hand,</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
